.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH instantmenu 1  "instantmenu 5.0.0"
.SH NAME
instantmenu \- A dynamic menu for X11 and Wayland (instantMENU, Rust port)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBinstantmenu\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-backend\fR] [\fB\-\-position\fR] [\fB\-\-follow\-cursor\fR] [\fB\-\-monospace\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-grab\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-outside\-close\fR] [\fB\-\-managed\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-x\-offset\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-y\-offset\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-monitor\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-prompt\fR] [\fB\-\-font\fR] [\fB\-\-line\-height\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-normal\-bg\fR] [\fB\-\-normal\-fg\fR] [\fB\-\-selected\-bg\fR] [\fB\-\-selected\-fg\fR] [\fB\-\-embed\fR] [\fB\-\-border\-width\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-reject\-no\-match\fR] [\fB\-\-toast\fR] [\fB\-\-single\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-input\-only\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-smart\-case\fR] [\fB\-\-match\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-pre\-match\fR] [\fB\-\-space\-confirm\fR] [\fB\-\-full\-height\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-insensitive\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-auto\-confirm\fR] [\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-alt\-tab\fR] [\fB\-\-right\-command\fR] [\fB\-\-left\-command\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-columns\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-lines\fR] [\fB\-\-placeholder\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-animation\-length\fR] [\fB\-\-preselect\fR] [\fB\-\-initial\-text\fR] [\fB\-\-frecency\-cache\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
instantmenu reads a newline\-separated list of items from stdin and displays them in a menu. Selecting an item and pressing Return prints it to stdout and exits; typing narrows the list to matching items.
.PP
The menu opens immediately and items stream in: the keyboard is grabbed before stdin is read, and the list grows as the input produces it (a fast producer collapses into a single refresh). With the `slide` subcommand it shows a value slider instead: Return prints the value and exits, every change runs \-\-command with the value appended.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH "WINDOW OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read appearance settings from this TOML file.

By default instantmenu reads $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/instantmenu/config.toml, falling back to ~/.config/instantmenu/config.toml. A missing default file is ignored.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-config\fR
Do not read the default appearance configuration file
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR [default: auto]
Backend to use: auto, x11 or wayland
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Auto\-detect: Wayland when WAYLAND_DISPLAY is set, else X11
.IP \(bu 2
x11: X11 (runs on Xwayland when started from a Wayland session)
.IP \(bu 2
wayland: Wayland (layer\-shell / xdg\-shell)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-position\fR \fI<POSITION>\fR
Anchor the menu to a corner, edge or the center of the screen
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
top\-left: Top\-left corner
.IP \(bu 2
top: Top edge, centered horizontally (the default)
.IP \(bu 2
top\-right: Top\-right corner
.IP \(bu 2
left: Left edge, centered vertically
.IP \(bu 2
center: Centered on the screen
.IP \(bu 2
right: Right edge, centered vertically
.IP \(bu 2
bottom\-left: Bottom\-left corner
.IP \(bu 2
bottom: Bottom edge, centered horizontally
.IP \(bu 2
bottom\-right: Bottom\-right corner
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-follow\-cursor\fR
Place the menu at the mouse position
.TP
\fB\-\-monospace\fR
Use a monospace font (Fira Code Nerd Font:pixelsize=15)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-grab\fR
Don\*(Aqt grab the keyboard
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-outside\-close\fR
Don\*(Aqt close the menu when clicking outside of it.

By default a modal menu (keyboard grabbed) closes on a click outside of it, like a GTK context menu.
.TP
\fB\-\-managed\fR
Let instantmenu be managed by the window manager as a normal window
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-x\-offset\fR \fI<N>\fR
Horizontal offset from the anchor position.

Positive moves right, negative moves left.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-y\-offset\fR \fI<N>\fR
Vertical offset from the anchor position.

Positive moves down, negative moves up.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR \fI<N|auto>\fR
Make instantmenu this wide.

`auto` sizes the menu to its content (the widest item plus the prompt).
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-monitor\fR \fI<N|auto>\fR
Select monitor by index.

Monitor numbers start from 0. `auto` follows keyboard focus, then uses the first monitor (the default). `\-\-follow\-cursor` explicitly selects the monitor containing the pointer.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-prompt\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Prompt added to the left of the input field (menu mode) or the slider label (slide mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-font\fR \fI<FONT>\fR
Font or font set (overrides the default)
.TP
\fB\-\-line\-height\fR \fI<N|auto>\fR
Minimum height of one menu line.

At least 8 pixels; `auto` derives it from the font.
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<THEME>\fR
Built\-in color theme.

`default` is an alias for `catppuccin`. Individual color options override the selected theme.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
catppuccin: Catppuccin Mocha (the default)
.IP \(bu 2
classic: The original instantMENU colors
.IP \(bu 2
gruvbox: Gruvbox Dark
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-normal\-bg\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Normal background color.

Supports #RGB, #RRGGBB, #RRGGBBAA and CSS color names.
.TP
\fB\-\-normal\-fg\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Normal foreground color.

Supports #RGB, #RRGGBB, #RRGGBBAA and CSS color names.
.TP
\fB\-\-selected\-bg\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Selected background color.

Supports #RGB, #RRGGBB, #RRGGBBAA and CSS color names.
.TP
\fB\-\-selected\-fg\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Selected foreground color.

Supports #RGB, #RRGGBB, #RRGGBBAA and CSS color names.
.TP
\fB\-\-embed\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Embedding window id (X11 only)
.TP
\fB\-\-border\-width\fR \fI<N>\fR
Border width.

Adds a border around the menu.
.SH "MENU MODE OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-reject\-no\-match\fR
Reject input if it results in no matches
.TP
\fB\-\-toast\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Toast mode that times out after SECONDS seconds.

The menu draws itself, waits the given time, then exits without a selection. 0 keeps the timeout disabled.
.TP
\fB\-\-single\-key\fR
Activate items by their explicit `key=` metadata.

Only keyed items are shown. Typing one key immediately prints that item\*(Aqs label; matching is otherwise disabled.
.TP
\fB\-\-input\-only\fR
Only display the input field, without the item list
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-smart\-case\fR
Enable smart case matching.

The pattern is matched case\-insensitively unless it contains an uppercase letter.
.TP
\fB\-\-match\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Item matching algorithm: fuzzy, dmenu or exact
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fuzzy: Fuzzy matching (the default): ranks by how tightly the pattern fits
.IP \(bu 2
dmenu: The classic dmenu matcher: every token must appear; exact, prefix, then substring matches are ranked in that order
.IP \(bu 2
exact: Only exact matches
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pre\-match\fR
Enable pre matching
.TP
\fB\-\-space\-confirm\fR
Confirm the selection with the space key
.TP
\fB\-\-full\-height\fR
Make instantmenu take the full screen height
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-insensitive\fR
Case\-insensitive item matching
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-auto\-confirm\fR
Auto\-confirm when exactly one item matches
.TP
\fB\-\-password\fR
Display input as dots
.TP
\fB\-\-alt\-tab\fR
Alt\-tab behaviour: cycle items with Alt+Tab.

While Alt is held, Tab advances to the next item and Shift+Tab goes back; releasing Alt confirms the selection, Alt+Space cancels the mode. Requires the keyboard grab (the default): without it the compositor keeps the keys and the menu never sees them.
.TP
\fB\-\-right\-command\fR \fI<CMD>\fR
Execute this command on shift + right arrow
.TP
\fB\-\-left\-command\fR \fI<CMD>\fR
Run this command on shift + left and add a click target left of the input field
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR \fI<N>\fR
Number of columns in grid mode.

Implies one line per row unless \-\-lines is given.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-lines\fR \fI<N>\fR
Number of lines in a vertical list
.TP
\fB\-\-placeholder\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Placeholder inside the input field
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-animation\-length\fR \fI<N>\fR
Animation length in frames
.TP
\fB\-\-preselect\fR \fI<N>\fR
Preselected item index.

Starts from 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-initial\-text\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Initial input text
.TP
\fB\-\-frecency\-cache\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Frecency cache: rank items by past selections and record new ones.

The value is a cache ID resolved under the XDG cache directory ($XDG_CACHE_HOME/instantmenu/<ID>, or ~/.cache/instantmenu/<ID>); an absolute path is used as the cache file directly. Distinct IDs hold independent histories (e.g. one per launcher).

On startup items are reordered best\-frecency first (stable — ties keep stdin order). Every printed selection — a chosen item or free\-typed text — is counted with a time decay and persisted. Not recorded: password input and slider values.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS instantmenu slide
Slide mode: show a value slider instead of a menu.

Return prints the current value to stdout and exits; Escape exits without printing. Every value change runs --command (if given) with the value appended as its last argument.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 0]
Minimum slider value
.TP
\fB\-\-max\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 100]
Maximum slider value
.TP
\fB\-\-value\fR \fI<N>\fR
Initial slider value.

Defaults to the middle of the range; clamped into it.
.TP
\fB\-\-step\fR \fI<N>\fR
Small step for left/right
.TP
\fB\-\-big\-step\fR \fI<N>\fR
Large step for up/down.

Defaults to a tenth of the range (at least 5).
.TP
\fB\-\-command\fR \fI<CMD>\fR
Command run on every value change (flag form of `COMMAND`)
.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
Command run on every value change.

Run through the shell with the current value appended as the last argument. Can be given as a positional argument or via \-\-command.

.SS instantmenu icons
Discover the Nerd Fonts icon names accepted by icon entries

.SH EXTRA
ITEM FORMAT:
  Each input line is a label. Optional leading `{...}` metadata is hidden
  from display and output: `{red icon=power key=q match=shutdown} Power off`.
  Attributes: color=NAME (or bare NAME), icon=NAME, key=CHAR,
  match=TEXT, value=TEXT, and heading. Quote values containing spaces. `{{` escapes a
  literal leading brace.

KEYBOARD CONTROL:
  Tab          copy the selected item to the input field
  Return       confirm the selection and exit
  Ctrl\-Return  confirm the selection and keep running
  Shift\-Return confirm the input text and exit
  Escape       exit without selecting an item
  Ctrl\-Left    move the cursor to the start of the current word
  Ctrl\-Right   move the cursor to the end of the current word
  C\-a Home  C\-b Left  C\-c Escape  C\-d Delete  C\-e End  C\-f Right
  C\-g Escape  C\-h Backspace  C\-i Tab  C\-j Return  C\-k delete right
  C\-m Return  C\-n Down  C\-p Up  C\-u delete left  C\-w delete word
  C\-y paste primary  C\-Y paste clipboard
  M\-b word start  M\-f word end  M\-g Home  M\-G End  M\-h Up
  M\-j page down  M\-k page up  M\-l Down  M\-F4 quit
ALT\-TAB MODE (\-\-alt\-tab):
  Alt+Tab      advance to the next item
  Shift+Tab    go back to the previous item
  release Alt  confirm the selection
  Alt+Space    cancel alt\-tab mode
SLIDE MODE (`slide`):
  Left h       decrease by \-\-step        Right l    increase by \-\-step
  Down j       decrease by \-\-big\-step    Up k       increase by \-\-big\-step
  plus/minus   change by 1               1..9, 0    jump to a ninth of the range
  Home         minimum value             End        maximum value
  Return       print the value and exit  Escape q   exit without printing
  click/drag   set the value at the pointer         wheel  step
  middle click reset to the initial value
.SH VERSION
v5.0.0
